# render_channel output
*.wav
*.csv

# ...but the simulator's golden files are the point, so they are tracked.
!sim/flows/golden/*.csv

__pycache__

# `just wasm` output. The generated panel spec and artwork under panel/ and
# web/ are tracked on purpose - they are derived from the hardware repo, which
# is not always to hand - but these two are built from sources in this repo by
# a recipe that every consumer already runs first.
web/bmcv.js
web/bmcv.wasm

# `just vcv` output. The plugin's own Makefile has to be exempted from the
# blanket `Makefile` rule above, which is there for in-source CMake builds.
!vcv/Makefile
vcv/plugin.so
vcv/plugin.dll
vcv/dist/
# A Rack SDK or a Rack install unpacked here for convenience. `just vcv-sdk`
# puts one outside the repo; this is for anyone who keeps theirs alongside.
vcv/rack/
